---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import StateLedger from "../components/StateLedger.astro";
import CtaBlock from "../components/CtaBlock.astro";
import { CHANNELS, getModules, moduleHref, pad, utm } from "../lib/course";

const modules = await getModules();
// Modules 00 and 10 carry written exercises rather than a lab, so the count is
// derived from the content instead of hardcoded.
const labCount = modules.filter((m) => m.data.lab).length;

const stack = [
  ["Python", "Plain Python first. You feel the loop before you are handed a runtime for it."],
  ["LangGraph", "Graph execution, state, persistence and interrupts as first-class runtime concepts."],
  ["FastAPI", "The run API and the review endpoints. Never run the graph inside the HTTP request."],
  ["PostgreSQL", "Checkpoints, event log, published reports. Durable state lives here, not on disk."],
  ["Neon", "Free managed Postgres from Module 03, so nothing changes at deploy time except env vars."],
  ["Render", "Free web service and git deploy, which is what makes the redeploy lab real."],
  ["HTMX", "The run dashboard and review screen with no build step and no client framework."],
];

const constraints = [
  ["Finite context leads to context rot.", "Performance degrades long before the hard token limit."],
  ["Compounding errors.", "A wrong fact in step 3 poisons step 40."],
  ["Models judge their own completeness poorly.", '"Done" from the model is a claim, not a fact.'],
  ["Everything grows with duration.", "Cost, latency, security surface, and drift from the original goal."],
  ["Failure is ambiguous.", "A timeout after a side effect leaves you not knowing whether the side effect happened."],
];
---

<Base
  title="Engineering Long-Running AI Agents | AIR Course 001"
  description="A free, open course on taking an agent from a simple loop to a durable production system: state, checkpoints, idempotency, failure taxonomies, human-in-the-loop, context engineering, observability and evals."
  pageSlug="home"
>
  <div class="shell">
    <section class="hero section">
      <p class="eyebrow">THE AI RUNTIME · COURSE 001 · FREE · OPEN SOURCE</p>
      <h1 class="hero__title">Engineering Long-Running AI Agents</h1>
      <p class="hero__sub">From a simple agent loop to a durable production system.</p>

      <div class="hero__grid">
        <div>
          <blockquote class="hero__quote">
            A long-running agent performs useful work whose lifecycle may outlive a single
            request, process, context window, worker, or human interaction.
          </blockquote>
          <p class="muted">
            The important property is not time. It is execution continuity. Thirteen modules,
            {" "}{labCount} Failure Labs, one boring application, and every failure reproducible
            on your machine.
          </p>
          <div class="hero__actions">
            <a class="btn btn--solid" href={moduleHref(modules[0]!)}>Start Module 00</a>
            <a class="btn" href="/labs/">See the {labCount} Failure Labs</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <StateLedger current={0} status="ready" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="thesis">
      <h2>Course thesis</h2>
      <div class="measure">
        <p>
          Anyone can build an agent that works once. This course is about what happens
          afterwards. Five constraints make long-running execution hard, and every module maps
          to one of them.
        </p>
      </div>
      <dl class="constraints">
        {
          constraints.map(([head, body]) => (
            <div class="constraints__row">
              <dt>{head}</dt>
              <dd>{body}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
      <p class="muted measure">
        Autonomy is not automatically desirable. Every step toward a free-running agent costs
        you predictability, testability and cost control. You should be able to say why you
        moved right.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="what-we-build">
      <h2>What we build</h2>
      <div class="build">
        <div class="measure">
          <p>
            One application for all thirteen modules: a <strong>Vendor Review Agent</strong>.
            Give it a vendor name and a URL, and it researches the vendor across their site and
            produces an evidenced brief against a fixed checklist.
          </p>
          <p class="muted">
            It is deliberately boring. The point is that every ounce of attention goes to the
            runtime, not to inventing features.
          </p>
        </div>
        <pre>{`CHECKLIST = [
    "product",
    "customer",
    "pricing",
    "security",
    "developer_experience",
    "unknowns",
]`}</pre>
      </div>

      <h3>What a finished run looks like</h3>
      <pre>{`Vendor: Acme

Requirements covered: 5/6
Unknown: Enterprise pricing

Evidence: 12 pages examined
Risks: 2
Estimated completeness: 83%

[Approve]   [Research missing items]   [Reject]`}</pre>
      <p class="muted measure">
        Human review needs evidence, not a yes or no. If the reviewer cannot see why the agent
        believes an item is verified, the review is theatre.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="why-this-example">
      <h2>Why this example</h2>
      <div class="measure">
        <p>
          The vendor brief is small enough to build in an evening and large enough to break in
          every way that matters. It has real fetches, real side effects, a human gate, an
          unbounded page space, and an output whose correctness is checkable.
        </p>
      </div>
      <pre>{`                LONG-RUNNING AGENT
                       │
        ┌──────────────┼──────────────┐
        ↓              ↓              ↓
      STATE        EXECUTION       CONTEXT
        │              │              │
   checkpoints       retry        compression
   progress          resume       artifacts
   evidence          timeout      handoff
        └──────────────┼──────────────┘
                       ↓
                    CONTROL
                       │
              human approval
              cancellation
              budgets
              permissions
                       ↓
                OBSERVABILITY
                       ↓
                  EVALUATION`}</pre>
      <p class="muted measure">
        State, Execution, Context, Control, Observability, Evaluation. Modules 02 to 09 take
        these one at a time, and Module 10 finds the same six primitives inside every credible
        production system.
      </p>
      <div class="measure">
        <p>
          Every lab runs against a deterministic fixture server, so "pricing returns 503 twice
          then 200" is one line of a profile file rather than a code change. Failures become
          reproducible, comparable and gradeable.
        </p>
      </div>
      <pre>{`git clone ${CHANNELS.repo}
cd air-course-001 && make fixtures   # deterministic vendor sites on :8001`}</pre>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="stack">
      <h2>Stack</h2>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table class="stack-table">
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Piece</th><th scope="col">Why it is here</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {stack.map(([name, why]) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{name}</th>
                <td>{why}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p><a href="/stack/">Why this stack, and the free hosting matrix &rarr;</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="syllabus">
      <h2>Syllabus</h2>
      <p class="muted measure">
        Thirteen modules in order. Read is always live. Watch turns on as each Failure Lab
        ships on YouTube, Notes as each longform ships on Substack.
      </p>

      <ol class="syllabus">
        {
          modules.map((m) => (
            <li class="syllabus__row">
              <div class="syllabus__num">{pad(m.data.module)}</div>
              <div class="syllabus__body">
                <h3 class="syllabus__title">
                  <a href={moduleHref(m)}>{m.data.title}</a>
                </h3>
                <p class="syllabus__goal">{m.data.goal}</p>
                {m.data.lab && (
                  <p class="syllabus__lab">
                    <span class="syllabus__lab-tag">FAILURE LAB {pad(m.data.module)}</span>{" "}
                    {m.data.lab}
                  </p>
                )}
              </div>
              <div class="syllabus__meta">
                <span class="meta">{m.data.duration}</span>
                <span class="syllabus__links">
                  <a href={moduleHref(m)}>Read</a>
                  {m.data.youtube ? (
                    <a href={utm(m.data.youtube, m.id, "watch")} rel="noopener">Watch</a>
                  ) : (
                    <span class="is-pending" aria-disabled="true" title="Video not published yet">Watch</span>
                  )}
                  {m.data.substack ? (
                    <a href={utm(m.data.substack, m.id, "notes")} rel="noopener">Notes</a>
                  ) : (
                    <span class="is-pending" aria-disabled="true" title="Longform not published yet">Notes</span>
                  )}
                </span>
              </div>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="different">
      <h2>How this course is different</h2>
      <div class="different">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--muted">ONE BORING APP</p>
          <p>
            Every module builds the same vendor agent. Nothing is a toy example that vanishes
            in the next chapter, so all the attention lands on durability instead of on a new
            domain each week.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--muted">FAILURE BEFORE ABSTRACTION</p>
          <p>
            You hit the failure first, on purpose, then get the primitive that fixes it.
            LangGraph does not appear until Module 03, after you have lost a run twice and
            felt exactly why a checkpointer exists.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--muted">EVALS ARE THE LOOP</p>
          <p>
            Not a plug-in at the end. Error analysis on real traces, binary criteria, a judge
            validated against human labels, and a regression gate that proves version B beats
            version A instead of preferring it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <CtaBlock slot="footer-cta" pageSlug="home" />
</Base>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: 4rem; }
  .hero__title {
    font-size: var(--t-hero);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .hero__sub {
    font-size: var(--t-h3);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .hero__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 2.5rem;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .hero__quote {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-body);
    color: var(--fg);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }
  .hero__actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .constraints {
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .constraints__row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.35rem;
    padding: 0.85rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .constraints dt {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-meta);
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .constraints dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--t-meta);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }

  .build {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .stack-table th[scope="row"] {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-meta);
    text-transform: none;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    color: var(--accent);
    white-space: nowrap;
    width: 10rem;
  }
  .stack-table td { color: var(--fg-muted); }

  .syllabus {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .syllabus__row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 3rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.35rem 1rem;
    padding: 1.25rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .syllabus__num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-meta);
    color: var(--accent);
    padding-top: 0.2rem;
  }
  .syllabus__title {
    font-size: var(--t-body);
    margin: 0 0 0.3rem;
  }
  .syllabus__title a { color: var(--fg); }
  .syllabus__title a:hover { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .syllabus__goal {
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
    font-size: var(--t-meta);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    max-width: 62ch;
  }
  .syllabus__lab {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-meta);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }
  .syllabus__lab-tag { color: var(--accent); letter-spacing: 0.06em; }
  .syllabus__meta {
    grid-column: 2;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem 1.25rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }
  .syllabus__links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-meta);
  }
  .is-pending {
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    opacity: 0.55;
    text-decoration: line-through;
    cursor: not-allowed;
  }

  .different {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 2rem;
  }
  .different p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; font-size: var(--t-meta); color: var(--fg-muted); }

  @media (min-width: 800px) {
    .constraints__row {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 22rem) minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 0.5rem 2rem;
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .hero__grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 26rem); gap: 3rem; }
    .build { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 24rem); gap: 2.5rem; }
    .different { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .syllabus__row { grid-template-columns: 3rem minmax(0, 1fr) 14rem; }
    .syllabus__meta {
      grid-column: 3;
      grid-row: 1;
      margin-top: 0;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-end;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
